478
00:59:41,700 --> 00:59:48,320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Meaning to say, it's beyond design because of the number of

479
00:59:48,500 --> 00:59:53,580
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: personnel we have to sustain the number of activities we do.

480
00:59:54,920 --> 00:59:59,500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That takes into account internal security, HADR...

481
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:03,220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and for joint exercises, retraining.

482
01:00:03,220 --> 01:00:14,220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: What suffers here is the amount of rest and retraining time that our men and women have.

483
01:00:15,800 --> 01:00:27,500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Right now, we do not have enough forces, both on the operational side to have adequate R&amp;R for them.

484
01:00:27,500 --> 01:00:32,260
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And secondly, we lack personnel on the support side.

485
01:00:33,400 --> 01:00:41,680
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The ratio of operating to support personnel is 80-20, more or less, which is unsustainable

486
01:00:41,680 --> 01:00:53,220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: because logistics, intelligence, planning, we need a robust infrastructure in order to sustain the operations.

487
01:00:57,500 --> 01:01:08,220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, the MOOE increase is much, much welcome, particularly, Your Honor, with the cost of fuel right now.

488
01:01:08,360 --> 01:01:15,100
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Last year, it is good that we were able to hedge the cost of fuel and assume that they would rise.

489
01:01:16,440 --> 01:01:23,400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, this year, the increase is relevant.

490
01:01:25,400 --> 01:01:27,400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: With capital outlay...

491
01:01:27,500 --> 01:01:31,420
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: With capital outlay, this is where our biggest gap is.

492
01:01:32,080 --> 01:01:37,780
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We need a lot of infrastructure right now, particularly, Your Honors, on the eastern seaboard,

493
01:01:38,320 --> 01:01:42,260
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: where we do not have naval presence.

494
01:01:42,600 --> 01:01:55,420
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We do not have substantial infrastructure also in Palawan, not for the naval purposes, but for the army purposes,

495
01:01:55,420 --> 01:01:57,420
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which will serve...

496
01:01:57,500 --> 01:02:01,140
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which will serve as hubs for supporting our strategic bases.

497
01:02:01,720 --> 01:02:02,260
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Mindoro.

498
01:02:03,260 --> 01:02:08,120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Our presence, too, in Mindoro is only one brigade.

499
01:02:09,420 --> 01:02:16,000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And with the size of Mindoro, Your Honor, that is not sufficient.

500
01:02:16,820 --> 01:02:21,940
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: In northern Luzon, we have only one division for how many provinces?

501
01:02:21,940 --> 01:02:25,940
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we only have one naval force.

502
01:02:26,680 --> 01:02:27,420
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: In that...

503
01:02:27,500 --> 01:02:31,600
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: In that area, which spans the South China Sea to the Pacific Ocean.

504
01:02:32,880 --> 01:02:41,420
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, we really need to refocus our strategic positioning in these areas, Your Honor.

505
01:02:41,560 --> 01:02:43,500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we cannot do that until...

506
01:02:44,360 --> 01:02:50,760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: sustainably, until the army solidifies its footprint in the Philippines.

507
01:02:50,760 --> 01:02:56,840
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, capital outlay, Your Honor, is extremely important.

508
01:02:57,500 --> 01:03:07,360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Also, for building critical infrastructure facilities for security of our platforms and security of our operations.

509
01:03:07,360 --> 01:03:22,200
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I believe the capital outlay gap has been one of the major gaps that we have found out right now we have to catch up badly with.

510
01:03:23,020 --> 01:03:27,360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And it includes also access to our bases.

511
01:03:27,500 --> 01:03:33,400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: In terms of the durability of the infrastructure.

512
01:03:33,720 --> 01:03:37,220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For example, the roads and bridges that will link our bases.

513
01:03:37,860 --> 01:03:46,860
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We have found that normal roads and bridges will not be able to support some of the platforms that we have currently because of the weight.

514
01:03:48,340 --> 01:03:51,920
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, our mobility is a sacrifice.

515
01:03:53,040 --> 01:03:56,500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We cannot really bridge the whole of the Philippines.

516
01:03:56,500 --> 01:03:56,660
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes.

517
01:03:57,500 --> 01:04:10,240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, the best that we can do is to provide hubs, as many hubs as possible, which will support sustained operations.

518
01:04:11,120 --> 01:04:20,540
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly, Your Honor, just like any other entity in the world right now, it's not a matter of just in time, but a matter of reserves and stores.

519
01:04:21,160 --> 01:04:26,280
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And that we are busy building up our reserve and stores.

520
01:04:26,480 --> 01:04:26,540
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Not only in...

521
01:04:27,500 --> 01:04:35,040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: In terms of munitions, but we need it also in terms of petroleum, oil, and lubricants.

522
01:04:35,040 --> 01:04:57,040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We have big notional amounts of petroleum ready, but if we do not have physical custody of this, we will be relying on private gas stations to serve our needs, which is a vulnerability of our operating troops.

523
01:04:57,580 --> 01:05:11,860
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And it poses difficulties for the troops rather than have them serviced in a durable basis, perhaps up to the battalion level.

524
01:05:15,120 --> 01:05:16,560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Next slide, please.

525
01:05:21,580 --> 01:05:26,560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The breakdown of regular fund versus...

526
01:05:27,500 --> 01:05:33,920
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The 2026 and 2027 comparatives, Your Honor.

527
01:05:36,920 --> 01:05:47,700
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, we have a slight increase of 6.13% versus last year of 18 billion.

528
01:05:49,540 --> 01:05:56,500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But I believe the increase is reflected more in MOOE.

529
01:05:57,500 --> 01:06:01,160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Than any other item.

530
01:06:01,760 --> 01:06:02,580
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Next slide, please.

531
01:06:10,380 --> 01:06:12,080
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Modernization, Your Honor.

532
01:06:12,960 --> 01:06:20,560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: 2026 was 90 with the programmed of 40 and unprogrammed of 50.

533
01:06:21,260 --> 01:06:24,080
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: This year, 50-50.

534
01:06:24,080 --> 01:06:24,160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thank you.

535
01:06:26,640 --> 01:06:27,240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Pensions.

536
01:06:27,500 --> 01:06:34,540
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Pensions have increased by 13.15%.

537
01:06:34,540 --> 01:06:40,520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Total.

538
01:06:42,520 --> 01:06:44,360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Next slide.

539
